 ## Background
-The Gaussian Normal Field Definition was introduced in "From Blobs to Spokes: High-Fidelity Surface Reconstruction via Oriented Gaussians" [S1]. It builds on the Objects as Volumes (OaV) framework, which provides an explicit expression for the gradient of the log-vacancy [S1]. The method is used to supervise oriented Gaussians during training to enforce proper surface wrapping and to extract meshes from the trained representation [S1].
+The Gaussian Normal Field Definition builds on [Analytical Vector Fields](3124-analytical-vector-fields.md) and was introduced in "From Blobs to Spokes: High-Fidelity Surface Reconstruction via Oriented Gaussians" [S1]. It leverages the Objects as Volumes (OaV) framework, which provides an explicit expression for the gradient of the log-vacancy [S1]. The method is used to supervise oriented Gaussians during training to enforce proper surface wrapping and to extract meshes from the trained representation [S1].
 
